The CI traces isolate the mode defect precisely: journals record POSIX source modes (`0444`/`0555`), while Windows reports writable staging as its canonical `0666`/`0777`; exact POSIX equality then treats the engine’s own chmod as foreign mutation. I’m checking the official Python Windows chmod/stat contract before encoding a canonical comparison, because the fix must retain the read-only bit as the mutation witness.
